<title>USA: TVA 1,170 MW Tenn. nuke back to full output.</title>
<headline>TVA 1,170 MW Tenn. nuke back to full output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tennessee Valley Authority's (TVA) 1,170 megawatt (MW) Watts Bar 1 nuclear power station returned to full output after its production was reduced late last week due to smoking insulation, the utility said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The condition stemmed from a small oil leak in the unit's feedwater pump.</p>
<p>Watts Bar 1, located between Chattanooga and Knoxville, Tenn., accounts for three percent of the company's total generation capacity.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1622</p>
